<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil gains, dollar firmer.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil gains, dollar firmer.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.8403)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     35.40/35.80     19.23/19.45   34.90/35.30</p>
<p> BREMEN		35.40/35.80     19.23/19.45   34.90/35.30</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    35.70/36.10     19.39/19.61   35.20/35.60</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   36.30/36.70     19.72/19.94   35.80/36.20</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   36.50/36.90     19.83/20.05   36.00/36.40</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  37.70/38.10     20.48/20.70   37.20/37.60</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices gained ground by between 40 and 50 pfennigs, reflecting a firmer screen and strong dollar. Demand was muted by the continuing firmness of the U.S. currency and higher futures values. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
